      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you give a little information about scenarios in which this will be better than KeystoneToken?\n\nI\u0027m having a little trouble wrapping my mind around it, because right now we have things like this:\n\n response \u003d PROVIDERS.token_provider_api.validate_token(token_id)\n return token_model.KeystoneToken(token_id\u003dtoken_id,\n                                  token_data\u003dresponse)\n\nToken data is directly associated with the token ID because of the way it\u0027s serialized. It seems like with the new model, we\u0027d have to do something like this:\n\n response \u003d PROVIDERS.token_provider_api.validate_token(token_id)\n token \u003d token_model.TokenModel()\n token.user_id \u003d response[\u0027user\u0027][\u0027id\u0027]\n if \u0027domain\u0027 in response:\n   token.domain_id \u003d response[\u0027domain\u0027][\u0027id\u0027]\n # etc \n token.mint(token_id, response[\u0027issued_at\u0027])\n\nA little more background on what this will unlock for us would be good.",
      "revId": "7ebcfdc9bf2a439a75db47277a49bb2432bd0663",
