      "writtenOn": "2018-06-21T15:59:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I opted to using the Bootstrap method here in favor of a couple different ways we duplicate the same process in test setup [0][1].\n\nThe token model changes don\u0027t have a hard dependency on using bootstrap, but I thought it would be a good opportunity to show an example of how we can re-use it in tests to provide us the same thing we do manually in a few places with setUp().\n\nI\u0027d like to try and make bootstrap the bedrock of our testing setUp, where applicable for tests that need it, and it should align our tests with what we tell operators to use (resulting in more rigorous testing of that tooling).\n\n[0] https://git.openstack.org/cgit/openstack/keystone/tree/keystone/tests/unit/test_v3.py?id\u003debd49159b41dbc2c97918f82aa860f87be7b5ed7#n240\n[1] https://git.openstack.org/cgit/openstack/keystone/tree/keystone/tests/unit/core.py?id\u003debd49159b41dbc2c97918f82aa860f87be7b5ed7#n710",
